You are working in /tmp/sv-835ed479a9e04189bee9cef7e9ff7b57/ShipmentTracker which is a Blazor Web App scaffolded with `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`. It has two projects: `ShipmentTracker` (server) and `ShipmentTracker.Client` (WebAssembly).

The app is for a logistics company that tracks shipments. Implement the following:

## 1. Remove template pages
Delete these files:
- ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Counter.razor
- ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Weather.razor

## 2. Create shared models in the .Client project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

## 3. Create service interface in .Client project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

## 4. Create HttpClient-based implementation in .Client project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentServiceClient.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentServiceClient(HttpClient httpClient) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        await httpClient.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
    }
}
```

## 5. Register HttpClient and service in Client Program.cs

Edit `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient("ServerAPI", client =>
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress));
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp =>
    sp.GetRequiredService<IHttpClientFactory>().CreateClient("ServerAPI"));
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServiceClient>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

## 6. Create server-side service implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServiceServer.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ShipmentServiceServer(IServiceScopeFactory scopeFactory) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        using var scope = scopeFactory.CreateScope();
        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContext>();
        return await db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        using var scope = scopeFactory.CreateScope();
        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContext>();
        return await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
    }

    public async Task UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        using var scope = scopeFactory.CreateScope();
        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContext>();
        var shipment = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
        if (shipment is not null)
        {
            shipment.Status = status;
            await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        }
    }
}
```

## 7. Add Shipment DbSet to ApplicationDbContext

Edit `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to add:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
```
And add this property to the class:
```csharp
public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
```

## 8. Update server Program.cs

Add these lines to `ShipmentTracker/Program.cs`:

After the existing service registrations (after `AddSingleton<IEmailSender...>`), add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServiceServer>();
```

You'll need to add these usings at the top:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Services;
```

Before `app.Run();`, add API endpoints:
```csharp
// Shipment API endpoints
var shipments = app.MapGroup("api/shipments").RequireAuthorization();

shipments.MapGet("/", async (ApplicationDbContext db) =>
    await db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync());

shipments.MapGet("/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
    await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber));

shipments.MapPut("/{id:int}/status", async (int id, ShipmentStatus status, ApplicationDbContext db) =>
{
    var shipment = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id);
    if (shipment is null) return Results.NotFound();
    shipment.Status = status;
    await db.SaveChangesAsync();
    return Results.Ok();
});
```

Also add these usings to the server Program.cs:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
```

